    "ecc_hypothesis": "PARTLY SETTLED by the A6000 run of 2026-11-12. That card reports ecc.mode.current=Enabled and, on a 48 GB GA102, nvidia-smi memory.total=46068 MiB / CUDA total=47,699,722,240 B -- byte for byte what the six slow A40s report, and 6.27% below the nominal 49,152 MiB. So the VRAM shortfall IS the ECC reservation, and the fast A40's 49,140 MiB (12 MiB below nominal) means ECC off. What the run does NOT explain is the ordering: the ECC-off A40 at 96.32 s is still faster than this ECC-on A6000 at 100.79 s despite 10.3% less nominal bandwidth, so ECC-off buys more than the capacity figure alone suggests, or that host differs in some further way. An ECC-on vs ECC-off pair on the same model would close it; no A5000 or 3090 is obtainable to try.",
    "rule": "compare arms only inside one pod and one session; a repeat on one card is good to ~3%, but the A40 pool is not one part",
